Browser DOM Static Bundle Demo
===============================================================================

The browser DOM demo is a complete static bundle project. It demonstrates configured browser host access, scoped DOM grants, an allowed DOM-to-Mech-to-DOM round trip, and a denied write.

1. Files
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

```text
examples/browser-dom-demo/
  README.md
  demo.mcfg
  demo.mec
  denied.mec
  index.html
```

2. Build the WASM package
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

```sh
cd src/wasm
wasm-pack build --target web
cd ../..
```

3. Bundle the project
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

```sh
mech bundle-web examples/browser-dom-demo --out dist/browser-dom-demo
python -m http.server 9000 -d dist/browser-dom-demo
```

Open:

```text
http://127.0.0.1:9000/
```

The bundle configuration declares `serve.paths`, `serve.shim`, and `serve.wasm`. The shim loads `./pkg/mech_wasm.js` and `./code/*.mec` with relative URLs, so it can run from a plain static web server.

4. What the demo shows
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The source binds the configured browser DOM context:

```mech
+> @browser := browser/dom
```

The allowed program reads the input, computes strings in Mech, and writes its result to configured DOM paths. `denied.mec` tries to write the read-only input and is rejected by its runtime grant.

For the maintained native/browser runtime example, use `mech run examples/analog-clock` or `mech serve examples/analog-clock`.
